कलम्बिका, f. the nape of the neck (in this sense
usually used in du.); the pot-herb Convolvulus Repens;
[cf. कलम्बी.]

कलुष कलुष, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. 1. कॄ?, said
to be fr. rt. 3. कल्), turbid, foul, muddy, unclean;
dark, opaque, without brilliancy; hoarse (as the
voice); wicked, bad; lazy, idle; (अस्), m. a buffalo;
(अम्), n. dirt, uncleanness; sin, wrath.
—कलुष-
ता, f. or कलुष-त्व, अम्, n. foulness, turbidness;
darkness, opacity; agitation, trouble, anger.
—कलु-
ष-योनि, इस्, इस्, इ, of impure origin.

कल्याणिन्, ई, इनी, इ, happy, lucky, prosperous;
illustrious; virtuous, good; (इनी), f. the water-plant
Sida Cordifolia.

कालीय, अस्, आ, अम्, relating to blackness; (अम्),
n. a dark kind of sandal or perhaps of Agallochum;
N. of a Nāga, see 1. कालिय above.

कालीयक, अस्, अम्, m. n. a species of aloe wood;
a kind of turmeric (Curcuma Xanthorrhiza?), a kind
of fragrant wood of a yellow colour; yellow sandal;
a dark kind of sandal-wood; (अस्), m., N. of a Nāga,
see 1. कालिय above.

कालकटङ्कट कालकटङ्कट, अस्, m. an epi-
thet of Śiva; (a various reading has शालकटङ्कट);
[cf. कटङ्कट.]

काल्याणिनेय काल्याणिनेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. कल्-
याणी), sprung from a virtuous or fortunate woman;
(अस्), m. the son of such a woman.
